{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אשת", :translit "eishet", :gloss "wife of / woman of"} {:he "בשר נבילה מאוסה", :translit "basar neveilah me'usah", :gloss "flesh of a nevelah, repulsive"} {:he "מוטב שיאכלו ישראל בשר תמותות שחוטות ואל יאכלו בשר תמותו נבילות", :translit "mutav sheyokhlu yisra'el basar temutot shchutot ve'al yokhlu basar temuto neveilot", :gloss "better that Israel eat meat of properly slaughtered carcasses and not eat meat of carcasses that died on their own"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אשת", :b "בשר נבילה מאוסה"}], :frame {:text "Kidushin 21b–22a derives from the phrase כי תראה בשביך אויב וחמדתה — 'when you see among the captives a beautiful woman' — that the soldier's desire for the captive woman is compared to a bodily appetite; the same passage connects the law of the beautiful captive to the framework of יצר הרע, the evil inclination. The phrase בשר נבילה מאוסה as a description of forbidden relations is used in Niddah 13b in the context of sins of the body. The specific drash that 'better Israel eat meat of properly slaughtered animals than meat of neveilot' is a homiletic formulation not located in a named canonical source.", :sources ["Kidushin 21b" "Kidushin 22a" "Niddah 13b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לך לאשה והבאתה אל תוך ביתך", :translit "lecha le'ishah uve'atah el toch beitecha", :gloss "to you for a wife and you shall bring her into the midst of your house"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Sequential reading of the verse: 'for a wife' follows the act of 'bringing her into your house,' understood as conversion first, then marriage."}], :frame {:text "Kidushin 21b derives from the sequence of the verse — 'you shall bring her into your house' (Deuteronomy 21:12) preceding 'she shall be your wife' (Deuteronomy 21:13) — that the captive woman must first undergo the conversion process before marriage is permitted. Sifrei Devarim 211 expounds the same sequence to establish that she must accept the commandments before the marriage takes effect.", :sources ["Kidushin 21b" "Deuteronomy 21:12" "Deuteronomy 21:13" "Sifrei Devarim 211"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "אשת", :a-value 701, :b "בשר נבילה מאוסה", :b-value 711, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Sequential reading of the verse: 'for a wife' follows the act of 'bringing her into your house,' understood as conversion first, then marriage.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:37:46.224485717Z", :model "glm-5.2"}